# r17-ct2-real-lane: CT-2 real-lane normal-priority post-settled surface reproduction.
#
# Reproduces the R17 plan at the real mock-LLM/Pi extension boundary:
#   1. Root lane: the root is its OWN pi process. It runs
#      through scripted turns that exercise the real swarm tool surface.
#   2. Worker turn is simulated via the test harness's deliverMessageLocked
#      call (see r17-ct2-real-lane.test.mjs scenario A/B/C). This is the
#      same durable-append code path the real worker would hit via
#      swarm_send_message(to=root, priority=normal, ...).
#   3. Five scripted turns: T0 baseline, T1 busy, T2 settled, T3 replay, T4 stop.
#
# Deterministic: scripted turns + delayMs gates. The boundary counter
# outcome table is printed by the test driver
# (extensions/swarm/r17-ct2-real-lane.test.mjs) after the lane completes.
# The companion tmux lane (tmux-snapshots/r17-ct2-validation/) repeats the
# same scenario via real two-pane Pi+mock-llm and captures pane before/after.
